request.user:
Resolve two candidate interpretations of one route-planning instruction. The instruction is the sole authority. Candidate agreement is not proof of correctness.

Return one JSON object only:
{"intent":{"pois":[],"time_limit":null,"dependencies":[],"quality_weight":0.5},"evidence":{},"changes":[]}

Evidence must quote short spans from the instruction. Changes must name every candidate field you revised. Do not use route efficiency to infer what the user wants.

Instruction:
Got to visit the library, supermarket, and bank today and be back by 18:00. Make sure supermarket comes before the bank, and focus on the fastest, most efficient route.

Candidate A:
{"dependencies": [["supermarket", "bank"]], "pois": ["bank", "library", "supermarket"], "quality_weight": 0.0, "time_limit": 1080}

Candidate B:
{"dependencies": [["supermarket", "bank"]], "pois": ["bank", "library", "supermarket"], "quality_weight": 0.0, "time_limit": 1080}

raw_response:
{
  "intent": {
    "pois": ["library", "supermarket", "bank"],
    "time_limit": 1080,
    "dependencies": [["supermarket", "bank"]],
    "quality_weight": 0.0
  },
  "evidence": {
    "pois": "library, supermarket, and bank",
    "time_limit": "be back by 18:00",
    "dependencies": "supermarket comes before the bank",
    "quality_weight": "fastest, most efficient route"
  },
  "changes": ["pois"]
}
